# DIR-124-A1a: per-run event log — transient diagnostic data, not committed provenance
.workflow-events/
# gap-no-explicit-blocked-signal-from-inner-layer (2026-08-03): the inner layer's explicit
# "I am stopped and waiting" signal — an existence signal in the same gitignored runtime-state
# family as gate-events.jsonl. File exists == inner is waiting; written only by
# inner-blocked-signal.ts (AC4), never by hand. It must stay untracked: it is a live control-plane
# signal that appears/disappears every time the inner layer stops and resumes.
**/.quay/inner-blocked.json
# gap-ruling-required-only-covers-outer-to-inner-not-manager-to-outer (2026-08-05): the parameterized
# observation primitive's namespaced signal + per-target observer counter for NON-inner targets
# (--target outer/manager writes .quay/blocked-signals/<target>.json + .<target>-observer-state.json).
# Same gitignored live control-plane family as inner-blocked.json/.ruling-observer-state.json — these
# files appear/reset every observation poll and MUST stay untracked (committing them would dirty the
# tree the transcript composite requires clean).
**/.quay/blocked-signals/
# gap-ruling-required-trigger-is-dead-code-never-wired-into-any-tick (2026-08-04): the pane
# observer's rolling multi-sample counter — same gitignored runtime-state family as inner-blocked.json.
# Must stay untracked: it is live observer state (consecutive needs-input samples) that advances and
# resets every 60s poll; committing it would dirty the tree the transcript composite requires clean.
**/.quay/.ruling-observer-state.json
